# Git workflow

`README.md` wins if this rule disagrees with it. There is no `CONTRIBUTING.md`.

## Branches and pull requests

- Target `main`. Create the feature branch from `main`.
- There is no pull request template. Describe the change in the pull request body.
- Open the pull request as a draft. Leave it draft until CI is green for the surface you touched.
- Do not put secrets, camera credentials, or stream URLs in the pull request body.
- Do not invent inboxes, team handles, or GitHub users.
- Do not deploy, and do not touch production, from a change that only updates rules or docs.
- Review the full branch diff (`git diff <base>...HEAD`), not only the latest commit.
- Push a new branch with `-u`.

## Commit messages

```
<type>: <description>

<optional body>
```

Types: feat, fix, refactor, docs, test, chore, perf, ci.

## Safety

- Do not pass `--no-verify`.
- Do not force-push shared branches, including `main`.
- Keep the hard lines in `common-security.mdc`: fail closed; no secrets in logs or responses; do not regenerate `ENCRYPTION_KEY`; do not delete `backend/data/app.db`; do not run `docker compose down -v`; do not let cleanup sweep named-entity thumbnails.

Run the tests for the surface you touched before asking for review. Commands are in `common-testing.mdc` and match `.github/workflows/ci.yml`.
